spec:
  grid: 16-25 rows x 10-16 cols, filled with bg=magenta(6)
  separator:
    color: grey(5)
    shape: single full-height vertical column
    position: places left_w in 5-11 and right_w in 2-4 (i.e. right side narrower than left)
  sprites:
    count: 2-5 black(0) connected components on the LEFT of the separator
    connectivity: 4-connected
    placement:
      rows: row-ranges of sprites are pairwise disjoint, separated by at least one full bg row
      cols: sprite bbox must fit strictly on left side (cols 0..sep-1); right edge NOT touching sep in general
      flush_with_sep: 0-1 of the sprites may already be flush (rightmost col == sep-1); rest are strictly left of sep-1
    shape:
      bbox: 2-8 rows x 2-6 cols
      size: 4-26 black cells
      interior: each sprite may contain 0-2 enclosed bg(6) "holes" (bg regions fully surrounded by black)
      symmetry: many sprites have LR and/or UD symmetry [observed]
    hole_trigger:
      most sprites (>=60%) contain at least one enclosed hole whose right-most cell would lie at column sep-2 AFTER sliding the sprite flush (i.e. hole touches the inner face of the right wall)
      such sprites are "ray emitters"; emitter sprites may have irregular outlines where some rows are narrower (right edge does NOT extend to sep-1), creating non-triggering enclosed holes; crucially the hole's right neighbor is the sprite's right edge at that row, and further right (toward sep-2) is bg — no black wall between hole and sep-2 [train[0], train[1]]
    non_emitter_distractor:
      non-emitter sprites include partial-hole distractors and solid blocks. Partial-hole types are structures adjacent to sep-2 that resemble holes but are NOT enclosed, including:
        - C-shape opening left (top+bottom bars + right wall, left wall missing): ███/··█/███
        - C-shape opening right (top+bottom bars + left wall, right wall missing): ███/█··/███
        - L-shape (right wall bar + one horizontal bar): ··█/··█/███
        - solid rectangles: small 2x2 or 3x3 blocks
      all non-emitter sprites must be single 4-connected components
  right_side:
    input: uniformly bg=magenta(6); NO other non-bg pixels
    output: for each sprite that emits, every row spanned by its triggering hole is painted red(2) across cols sep+1..w-1 on the right side
  output_left:
    every sprite is translated rightward by (sep-1 - max_col) so its right edge is flush with sep-1
    original sprite pixels are erased to bg; separator and right side untouched except red rays

generation_strategy: |
  Output-first (since slid/enclosed configuration is the constrained state):
  1. Pick grid h in [16,25], w in [10,16]; choose sep in [5,11] ensuring right_w = w-sep-1 in [2,4].
  2. Fill grid with bg=6; set column sep to 5.
  3. Choose n_sprites in [2,5]. Partition row range into n disjoint vertical bands separated by >=1 bg row.
  4. For each band, build a sprite (bbox 2-8 x 2-6):
     - With prob ~0.7, design a closed rectangular-ish shell around a 1-2 wide hole so that its right wall sits at col sep-1 and the hole's rightmost cells lie at sep-2 (triggering emitter). Optionally add LR/UD symmetry.
     - Otherwise make a non-emitter distractor: C-shape (open left or right), L-shape (bar + one cross-bar), or small solid block. Must be 4-connected. These have bg at sep-2 surrounded by 2-3 black neighbors but NOT enclosed.
     - Pick a left-offset so the sprite fits (cols in [0,sep-1]); rightmost column is set to sep-1 for most sprites (flush by construction).
  5. Stamp sprite black pixels on left half. This is the OUTPUT left half.
  6. For each emitter sprite, for every row r containing a hole pixel at col sep-2, paint output[r, sep+1:w] = red(2). This gives the OUTPUT.
  7. Derive INPUT by un-sliding: for each sprite independently, choose a random leftward shift delta in [0, sep-1 - bbox_width] (with delta>=1 for at least n-1 sprites); translate its black pixels by -delta columns on the left half. Right side stays all bg. Erase any red rays. Keep separator column unchanged. Return the resulting grid as input.
  Self-check: separator is full-height, sprites fit on left, >=1 sprite is an emitter, right_w in [2,4], row-bands disjoint.
```
